// ServUO: RevampedSpawns/BlackthornDungeonCreature.xml (44 rows) and BlackthornDungeonAgent.xml (10 rows), the
// XmlSpawner definitions ServUO's [GenBlackthorn loads with "[XmlLoad RevampedSpawns/..." (cc-P196), carried as data,
// one row per <Points> element, in file order (generated by gen_spawns.py and gen_spawn_file.py, notes).
//
// XmlSpawner -> ModernUO Spawner, field by field (the P194 WrongSpawns shape; every value below is the XML's):
//   <Name>                     Name: "Spawner_Blackthorn" (the dungeon's 44: 22 per facet, the same multiset) or
//                              "AgentOfTheCrown" (the ten turn-in NPCs: nine Felucca cities and the Trammel castle).
//   <Map>                      Felucca flag; the spawner and its spawns go on that facet.
//   <CentreX/Y/Z>              Location.
//   <X> <Y> <Width> <Height>   SpawnBounds, the rectangle spawns land in, at full Z range like ModernUO's own
//                              legacy import (BaseSpawner.cs:323-341). The Agent rows are 0x0 (XmlSpawner spawns on
//                              the tile itself); pinned bounds need one tile.
//   <Range>                    WalkingRange, which Spawn() writes to the creature's RangeHome.
//   <IsHomeRangeRelative>      SpawnLocationIsHome (true on every row).
//   <MaxCount>                 Count.  <MinDelay>/<MaxDelay>: the dungeon rows are in seconds (DelayInSec True,
//                              60-150 s), the Agent rows in minutes (5-10, carried as 300-600 s).
//   <Objects2> type:MX=n       one entry per type, probability 100, maxCount n; two or three entries on seven rows.
//                              No constructor arguments anywhere. Type names are the XML's, case-corrected
//                              (exodusminion, golemcontroller, golem, giantrat, vampirebat).
//   <SmartSpawning>            True on all 44 dungeon rows; no counterpart (D-34's shape: the dungeon is populated
//                              whether or not anyone is in it). False on the Agent rows.
//   Everything else            XmlSpawner defaults (no triggers, no sequential spawning, no despawn, KillReset 1).
//
// Capacity: each entry is capped at its own maxCount, so a row never holds more than the sum of its entries; here
// every row asks for exactly its entries' sum (208 creatures on both facets, 104 each; the test derives it).
//
// Every creature type is stock pinned ModernUO (HellHound, Skeleton, ExodusMinion, GiantSpider, Brigand,
// GolemController, Golem, EvilMage, EvilMageLord, Lich, Dragon, Drake, GreaterDragon, FrostOoze, SnowElemental,
// GoldenElemental, RottingCorpse, EarthElemental, GiantRat, VampireBat, Balron); AgentOfTheCrown is this port's.
//
// cc-P691: the table stays ServUO's (stock coordinates, both facets); Generate places what stands now. The 22 Trammel
// dungeon rows go on the Fold, centre and bounds through BlackthornFold.Move (the dungeon proper's piece). The Trammel
// Agent stands in the author's Blackthorn Castle by the cellar hatch (BlackthornFold.AgentSpot; ServUO's 1488,1473 is
// the castle's moat on SoS). The Felucca rows are not placed: one dungeon, and no Felucca city spot is checked on SoS.

using System;
